# NPU model artifacts and the Qualcomm SDK.
#
# Two reasons, not one. Size — a context bundle is gigabytes. And licence: the
# Qualcomm runtime's grant covers redistribution "as incorporated in Your
# software application" and explicitly NOT "on a standalone basis", so a
# checked-in .aar/.so would be standalone redistribution — and would fold
# proprietary code into an MIT repository. Gradle resolves it from Maven at
# build time instead. See docs/NPU-BACKEND.md.
# Generated NPU context bundles (metadata.json + *.bin shards + tokenizer, or
# the AI Hub .zip). Gigabytes each, and not ours to redistribute.
*.bin
*.pte
*.serialized
*.dlc
genie_bundle/
genie_bundle*/
**/npu-artifacts/
**/npu-bundles/

# Qualcomm SDK / runtime binary drops. The build resolves geniex-android from
# Maven Central; nothing here looks for a hand-copied SDK, and a manually
# dropped binary is exactly the standalone redistribution the licence excludes.
qairt/
qnn-sdk/
qnn-runtime/
geniex-sdk/
GenieX/
**/libQnn*.so
**/libgeniex*.so
*.aar

# AI Hub credentials. Never commit a token.
.qai-hub/
.qai_hub/
**/.qai_hub/client.ini
qai_hub_token*
*.aihub-token
QAI_HUB_API_TOKEN*

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Claude Code
.claude/
